CORE
template-quoted.sh
--resolve-dynamic-sites --cvc5
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[shell-dynamic-site\.1\] .*: SUCCESS$
^\[shell-unsupported\.1\] .* the parts of the text of eval for the holes of .* have no character .*: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.1\] .* = "pre\$\{x\}'z": SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A hole in single quotes whose part has '\'', as quoting a value for the
shell makes: the ghost variable holds the part with each '\'' replaced
by '. (With refined strings, a part with ' is reported instead.)
